## 3. Detailed Physical & Numerical Evaluation Across Core Metrics

### 3.1 Force-Displacement Response ($F-u$) & Initial Stiffness ($K_0$)
- **Linear Elastic Regime ($0 \le u \le 0.0025\,\text{mm}$)**:
  * The harmonized fixed baseline (`1401091`) exhibits $K_0 = 134.46\,\text{kN/mm}$ ($R^2 = 0.99999998$).
  * The clamped fixed baseline (`1398090`) exhibits $K_0 = 138.09\,\text{kN/mm}$ ($+2.70\%$ higher stiffness due to lateral constraint on the top edge).
  * The empirical 2.0% adaptive model (`1400395`) matches the linear response with $K_0 = 137.84\,\text{kN/mm}$ ($-0.11\%$ vs clamped, $+2.51\%$ vs harmonized).
  * In contrast, the nominal 1.0% over-refined model (`1399632`) suffers an anomalous early compliance drop ($K_0 = 122.38\,\text{kN/mm}$, $-11.29\%$ error), caused by widespread early degradation across the excessively dense mesh.

### 3.2 Peak Reaction Force ($F_{\max}$) & Displacement at Peak ($u(F_{\max})$)
